fact WorkItem(id: "WI-716", description: some(value: "Loader stores an absent OPTIONAL entity field as an unbound fresh var in GROUND FACTS, which is unsound under SLD unification. Root cause (per user): the fresh-var fill in the loader's partial-named-arg expansion (kb/load.rs:6969 fact/rule path + :5314 query path) is the PATTERN representation of an entity — \"specify a few fields, the rest match anything\" — and it has leaked into ENTITY (fact/value) representation. In a ground fact an absent optional field means none(), but it is stored as Var(fresh), so the fact is logically \"forall v. Entity(field: v)\" and unifies with some(?), none(), or anything.\n\nCONFIRMED REPRO (anthill query --resolve): entity Thing(id: String, note: Option[String]); fact Thing(id: \"A\", note: some(\"hello\")); fact Thing(id: \"B\") with note OMITTED; rule has_note(?id, ?n) :- Thing(id: ?id, note: some(?n)). Query has_note(?id, ?n) returns 2 solutions — {A, \"hello\"} (correct) AND {B, ?_} (SPURIOUS, ?n unbound) — instead of 1. B has no note yet matches some(?n).\n\nIMPACT: any rule/query matching an Option field by some/none structure is unsound against a fact that omits that field. Latent in examples/github-todo only because its queried optionals (description, depends_on) are always written explicitly; the omitted optionals (context, generates, requires_capability) are stored as vars but never matched. rules.anthill matches \"description: some(?desc)\" (:39/44/50) and \"depends_on: nil()/cons(...)\" (:20/23) — these misfire the moment an Open item omits the field.\n\nNOTE the existing materialize->none() promotion (materialize_entity, eval/builtins.rs:1454, the WI-267 Var-valued-Option->none() branch) does NOT fix this: it only corrects the value READ path (Term->Value::Entity); SLD unifies the stored TERM, whose optional slot is still a var.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: split the entity VALUE conversion from the entity PATTERN conversion.\n- entity value (fact-assert path, load.rs:6969 when lowering a `fact` head — thread a \"this is a ground fact\" flag, or normalize the fact term at assert time): absent optional field -> none() (detect via kb::typing::is_option_type); absent REQUIRED field -> loud load error, not a silent var.\n- entity pattern (convert_query_term load.rs:5314; rule-body atoms): KEEP var-fill — \"unspecified = matches anything\" is correct for a pattern.\nBoth stay discrim-tree aligned: a none()-valued fact slot still unifies a pattern's var (so Thing(id: ?) finds B), but correctly fails note: some(?n).\n\nOnce facts store none() directly, evaluate whether materialize_entity's WI-267 Var-valued-Option branch can be narrowed (keep it only for residual var-bearing rule/pattern terms).\n\nDOC: documented in docs/design/entity-term-mapping.md (Rule 3 and section 3 fact-vs-query). That doc currently presents the var-fill as intended for both fact and pattern — update it once this lands (and until then it should flag the smell).\n\nACCEPTANCE: the repro query returns exactly 1 solution (only A); an integration regression test asserts an omitted-optional fact does NOT match a some(?) pattern (and a none() pattern DOES match); cargo-test green. Surfaced during WI-268's doc review."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-13T17:49:10Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-716", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED. Root fix: the loader's absent-named-field fill now keys on VALUE vs PATTERN position, not \"is a fact\". In a value position an absent OPTIONAL field is filled with none() (value semantics); a pattern keeps the fresh-var fill (\"matches anything\"). Mechanism: a `Loader.in_value_position` flag (renamed from an initial fact-only `in_fact_value`), set by load_fact (fact head) AND load_rule (each rule head), read by the partial-named-arg expansion (kb/load.rs). none() is built as Fn{Option.none} which alloc canonicalizes to Ref(none) (WI-511), identical to a user-written none(). Absent REQUIRED fields still var-fill (unchanged; malformed-fact hardening left out of scope).\n\nSCOPE GREW DURING /code-review — two adversarial reviewers refuted the initial fact-only fix on two counts, both confirmed empirically and now fixed:\n (Concern 1) an entity-DERIVING rule head (`rule Thing(id: ?id) :- src(?id)`) also produces a value, so its omitted optionals must be none() too — the fact-only fix left the same bug reachable through rule heads. Fixed by setting in_value_position for rule heads.\n (Concern 3) a reflect `Term`-typed field holds a QUOTED PATTERN, not a value (e.g. FactHolds(pattern: E(id: ?x))); none()-filling inside it over-restricts the pattern to none()-valued matches — a regression the fact-only fix introduced. Fixed by `convert_arg_value`, which clears in_value_position when recursing into a reflect.Term field. Applied at all three reflect-Term positions: a bare `Term` field, an `Option[Term]` payload (via the named-arg path), and a `List[Term]` element (via the list-element path).\n\nThe value flag propagates through the whole value recursion (so nested value entities like ToolPasses.params get none()) but resets to pattern at every reflect.Term boundary.\n\nTESTS: 4 regression tests in tests/include/wi716_optional_fact_none_fill_test.rs — (1) omitted-optional fact does NOT match some(?) [core]; (2) a pattern omitting the field still matches all [no over-restriction]; (3) entity-deriving rule head stores none() [Concern 1]; (4) reflect Term field keeps a var, not none() [Concern 3]. List[Term] element routing verified empirically (anthill query) + covered by the broad suite. Golden transcript updated: `show`'s acceptance now prints `ToolPasses(tool: \"cargo-test\", params: none)` instead of the leaked loader var `params: ?params` — the bug had been surfacing in user-facing CLI output. is_reflect_term_type made pub(crate).\n\nVERIFIED: full workspace suite green (74 binaries, 2801 passed, 0 failed) across the final change. Empirical anthill-query repros confirm: fact omitted-optional => 1 match (was 2); entity-deriving rule => 0 (was 1); reflect Term / List[Term] patterns keep their var.\n\nNOTES / possible follow-ups (not filed):\n - rules.anthill matches optionals structurally (`depends_on: nil()`/`cons(...)`, `description: some(?)`). Now that an OMITTED optional is none() (not a wildcard var), such a rule won't match a fact that omits the field. Currently latent — all 196 workitems.anthill facts write depends_on and description explicitly. If a future fact omits one, the rule needs a `none()` case (or the fact should write the value).\n - A pre-existing WI-697 order-dependence (a nullary constructor keys as Fn{c} before / Ref(c) after option.anthill registers `none` as a constructor): WI-716 removes the spelling-independence that made omitted-field fills immune. Not triggered under normal alphabetical load (user code loads after the full prelude; no pre-option.anthill facts have Option fields). Robust fix would register some/none as constructors in register_prelude.\n\nDesign doc docs/design/entity-term-mapping.md updated (section 3 + Rule 3) to describe value-position vs pattern-position semantics.", at: "2026-07-13T17:49:11Z")
